## Context
Audit: `conception/2026-10-29-memory-system-audit.md` (PR #1984) §4.2, R6. On padme since 2026-10-15, Claude Code main sessions made 0 `Read` calls on
`memory/MEMORY.md` or `memory/topics/` (audit: 0 of 148; lair session recheck: 0 of 106 in the
harness project dir, with a positive control matching Read calls in 26). Codex read them in 77%
of 468 sessions; Pi had 4 sessions. Nobody has measured whether reading topics helps.
Recent research (VibeMemBench; "Useful Memories Become Faulty", May 2026) makes a null result plausible.

## Scope
- Extend `scripts/census/memory-recall.py` to repository memory paths on Claude Code, Codex and
  Pi, on padme and doudou, including subagent transcripts (team-lead briefs should name topics
  by path: `rules/workflow.md` § Delegation).
- One small outcome trial: the same ten harness tickets with and without topics, judged on
  rework and reviewer findings. Price the model spend before running.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The census reports read counts per runtime and host, with a positive control
- [ ] The trial result is written in `conception/` with its arithmetic and its limits

## Native auto-memories as benchmarks (author, 2026-10-29)
The author asked to treat the Claude Code and Codex auto-memories as benchmarks, both as
outcome-trial arms and as reference designs. State on padme, 2026-10-29:
- Claude Code: on. 1,183 notes across project dirs under `~/.claude/projects/*/memory/`,
  for example AEDIST-technical-report 199 notes (804 KB), search-works-for-zotero 145 (640 KB),
  climate-finance-het 123 (528 KB), the harness 28. These are directory sizes, not injected
  bytes. Only each MEMORY.md index is loaded at start; notes are read on demand. The large
  stores suggest the same accumulation the repository store shows; not yet checked note by note.
- Codex: the `memories` feature reports `stable`, `false` (`codex features list`, CLI 0.165.0).
  `~/.codex/memories_1.sqlite` holds 0 rows. Its schema has a two-phase pipeline (per-thread
  `stage1_outputs` with `raw_memory` and `rollout_summary`, then a consolidation with
  `selected_for_phase2`), and it keeps `usage_count`/`last_usage` per memory, a decay signal
  the repository store lacks. Enabling it is a user-settings change: the author's act.

Trial arms (the same ten harness tickets):
1. no memory (native memories off, no repository memory);
2. Claude Code native auto-memory only;
3. Codex native memories only (after the author enables the feature and it has warmed up on past threads);
4. repository memory (departments, after 1349) only;
5. repository memory with native memory, as today.
Judge on rework, reviewer findings and repeated incidents; report tokens injected per arm.

Design comparison to report alongside: capture (automatic or roar), consolidation (Codex's two
phases versus smelt), retirement and decay (usage counts versus none), size bounds, and
cross-runtime reach (each native store serves one runtime; the repository store serves all three).

## More reference designs (author, 2026-10-29)
Web survey, lair session 2026-10-29 (sources: official docs unless marked).
- **Claude Code** (code.claude.com/docs/en/memory): auto memory is keyed by git repository and
  shared by worktrees; the first 200 lines or 25 KB of MEMORY.md load at start, topic notes on
  demand; the only built-in upkeep is an index-size reminder ("merge or drop stale entries").
  `autoMemoryDirectory` is read from any settings scope, project included. Subagents do not get
  the main auto memory; an agent's `memory: user|project|local` gives it its own store
  (`project`: `.claude/agent-memory/<agent>/`, under version control). "Auto Dream" background
  consolidation appears only in third-party reports; the official page does not mention it.
- **Qwen Code** (qwenlm.github.io/qwen-code-docs, users/features/memory): the most complete runtime
  design found. Managed auto-memory (on by default, four note types, `~/.qwen/projects/<project>/memory/`);
  `pinned/` notes that upkeep never touches; documented Dream consolidation (about daily after
  enough sessions, `/dream`); opt-in team memory in `.qwen/team-memory/` shared through git with a
  secret scan and per-write approval; opt-in sync that commits and pushes only that directory.
- **Mistral**: Vibe has no built-in memory (local check of 2.26.0 and its docs). Le Chat
  Memories (consumer, beta): explicit and automatic saves, recall shown with a link to its
  source, every entry editable.
- **Other Chinese runtimes**: Kimi Code has `AGENTS.md` layers and sessions, with memory through
  plugins (secondary sources); iFlow CLI, Trae and GLM/ZCode have none found (MCP or Mem0 add-ons).
- **ReMe** (Alibaba AgentScope, github.com/agentscope-ai/ReMe, Apache-2.0): v0.4.2.0 (2026-10-26) added automatic
  memory plugins for Claude Code and Codex. Markdown files with frontmatter and wikilinks in a
  local `.reme/` workspace: `session/`, `daily/`, `digest/personal|procedure|wiki/`;
  `auto_memory` capture, `auto_dream` consolidation ("creates, corroborates, refines, or corrects"
  digest nodes), BM25 with optional embeddings. The README shows no decay, deletion or size policy.
  Self-reported: LongMemEval cleaned-s 89.4%, BEAM 66.1% at 100K.
  ReMe is a candidate trial arm: it is the one off-the-shelf store that spans Claude Code and Codex.
